3.9. Blockchain-based integrity verification and fault recovery
The blockchain-based integrity verification module, illustrated in Fig. 5, was incorporated to provide secure, transparent, and tamperresistant storage of diagnostic predictions generated by the proposed CNN–Transformer framework. Following smartwatch-based inertial signal acquisition and model inference, each prediction record is converted into a blockchain transaction and processed through a lightweight Ethereum-inspired blockchain layer. Unlike conventional centralized storage systems, blockchain maintains a distributed ledger in which every transaction is cryptographically linked to preceding records, thereby ensuring immutability and traceability of diagnostic outcomes. To secure prediction records, the framework employs the Secure Hash Algorithm (SHA-256) to generate a unique fixed-length cryptographic hash for each transaction. The generated hash acts as a digital fingerprint of the prediction and is stored within a blockchain block together with a timestamp and the hash of the previous block. The hashing operation is expressed as:
